.TH SHB-RESTORE 1 "October 2026" "SecretHarbor 0.4.0-prod" "SecretHarbor Manual"
.SH NAME
shb-restore \- Restore real secret files from a legacy in-place swap session
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBshb restore [path] [--all] [--orphans]\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Restores real secret files for legacy in-place swap sessions (pre-shadow-workspace versions) or after an interrupted session. Modern sessions use shadow workspaces on macOS and mount virtualization on Linux, which never modify real files, so no restore is required.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB-a\fR, \fB--all\fR
Restore all registered legacy swap sessions
.TP
\fB-o\fR, \fB--orphans\fR
Restore orphaned legacy swaps left by crashed or terminated processes
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
$ \fBshb restore\fR
.TP
$ \fBshb restore --all\fR
.TP
$ \fBshb restore --orphans\fR
.TP
$ \fBshb restore /path/to/project\fR
.SH SEE ALSO
shb(1)
.SH WEBSITE
https://secretharbor.dev
